# These requests follow the contract in libs/contract; docs/reference/openapi.json is generated from it.
@backend = http://localhost:8080
@web = http://localhost:3000

### Backend: liveness (no dependencies, run with `npx nx dev flash-be`)
GET {{backend}}/health

### Backend: readiness (checks Postgres and Redis, needs `npx nx db:up flash-be`)
GET {{backend}}/ready

### Web: health check (Start server route, run with `npx nx dev flash-web`)
GET {{web}}/api/health

### Backend: the current sale (the sale that opens last, up to SALE_CACHE_MS old; seed one with `npx nx db:seed-sale flash-be --stock=100`)
GET {{backend}}/sales/current

### Backend: one sale by id (replace the id with the one the seed command printed)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### Backend: join the queue (replace the sale id; the reply holds your ticket; write requests can answer 429 with Retry-After)
POST {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "ana" }

### Backend: check your place (send the ticket from the join reply)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue/ana
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here

### Backend: reserve one item (needs the ticket and an admitted user; the reply holds the reservation id and its end)
POST {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/reservations
Content-Type: application/json
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here

{ "userId": "ana" }

### Backend: pay for the held item (send the reservation id from the reserve reply; sending it again is safe)
POST {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "ana", "reservationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001" }

### Backend: did I get it? (purchased, holding or none)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/purchases/ana

### Backend: live sale status (Server-Sent Events; stays open, sends an event when the sale changes)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/events

### Backend: live place in the queue (send the ticket from the join reply; stays open)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue/ana/events
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here

### Web: the current sale through the pass-through route (what the page calls; run with `npx nx dev flash-web`)
GET {{web}}/api/sales/current

### Web: join the queue through the pass-through route (replace the sale id; the reply holds your ticket)
POST {{web}}/api/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "ana" }

### Web: reserve one item through the pass-through route (send the ticket from the join reply)
POST {{web}}/api/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/reservations
Content-Type: application/json
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here

{ "userId": "ana" }

### Web: pay for the held item through the pass-through route
POST {{web}}/api/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "ana", "reservationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001" }

### Web: did I get it? through the pass-through route
GET {{web}}/api/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/purchases/ana

### Web: a path that is not allowed answers 404 not_found
GET {{web}}/api/sales/current/secret
